 config-load entrypoint that resolves the effective type map once for the whole pass before the mutation loop begins","AC 'test_load_time_fail_closed_on_undecided_syncable_type' pins the raise but not the pass-level ordering that 'before any mutation' requires"],"finding":"The plan states the completeness gate raises 'AT RESOLUTION (load) time, before any mutation', but the mirrored resolver (effective_status_map) is invoked lazily per-ticket DURING mutation computation (_effective_status_map_for inside the differ loop), not at a single distinct config-load checkpoint. The plan does not name the invocation site that guarantees the gate fires before ANY mutation is emitted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7dfbdc0b9d7cf95d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Finding 1 (G7) — 'raise MappingConfigError AT RESOLUTION (load) time, before any mutation'","norm_id":"n11e9daebe5657d0a","priority":0.75,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A pass where the first project's tickets are decidable and produce mutations, then a later ticket's project resolves to an undecided type — the gate fires only when that ticket is reached, AFTER earlier mutations were already computed/emitted"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Specify a pre-pass resolution step (e.g. resolve+validate the effective type decision for every project represented in local_tickets at the top of compute_outbound_mutations, before the :426 loop) so an undecided syncable type aborts the pass prior to any mutation, consistent with the offline mapping_config.validate fail-closed model.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_m