n cites only the coerce at :86 inside `_map_local_to_dc_fields`."],"finding":"Finding 4's patch-site inventory for the `type_map` threading through `map_local_to_remote` omits `adapters/jira/backend.py:73` `_JiraOutbound.map_local_to_remote` (and does not name the `_DCOutbound.map_local_to_remote` wrapper at `jira_datacenter/backend.py:121`, citing only the module-level coerce at :86). The Protocol `map_local_to_remote` has three implementers, but the plan lists only the Protocol, `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields`, and the DC module-level function.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f31f2581283c65c27","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Finding 4 (G6) — thread the effective type map through the Backend port","norm_id":"n8e38f3ae358df41e","priority":0.7556,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["`adapters/jira/backend.py:73` `_JiraOutbound.map_local_to_remote` left unedited: the Cloud port never accepts or forwards `type_map`, so `_map_local_to_jira_fields` receives `None` and the per-project effective type map never drives Cloud create issuetype — the finding's threading silently under-delivers on the Cloud path.","`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:121` `_DCOutbound.map_local_to_remote` wrapper signature not updated: even with the :86 coerce replaced, the wrapper does not pass `type_map` into `_map_local_to_dc_fields`, so the DC create path receives no effective map."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In Finding 4, enumerate all three `map_local_to_remote` bodies: the Protocol at `_backend.py:372`, the Cloud `_JiraOutbound` at `adapters/jira/backend.py:73` (add `type_map` param and pass it to `_map_local_to_jira_fields`), and the DC `_DCOutbound` at `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:121` (add `type_map` param and pass it to `_map_local_to_dc_fields`, whose :86 coerce is replaced).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"y